# wire: a jumper of wire at the bench. The DIP in the vise; the wire
# feeder station S5 feeds 40 mm of AWG 26 toward the work; the arm takes
# the wire by its middle and S5 cuts it at the nozzle; the arm brings
# the wire's end to pin 3, and pincer P1 grips it there; the turntable
# presents the joint to the iron station, which solders it; pincer P2
# bends the wire's other half down, toward where its next part will be.
reset circuit=demo
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=0,0,90
vise close
release A U1
lift A mm=60
wire S5 awg=26 mm=40
pick A W1 grasp=middle
cut S5
lift A mm=60
move A to=0,60,60 rpy=180,0,-45
move A to=17.952,15.412,-11.365
align A W1.1.tip to=U1.3.2.5 gap=0.1
pinch P1 on=W1.1 at=12
release A W1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+W1.1 at=S1
scope aim=U1.3+W1.1 zoom=8
touch S1 at=U1.3+W1.1 dwell=2
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+W1.1 below=100
scope aim=W1.2 zoom=3
bend P2 on=W1.2 at=6 angle=90 toward=0,0,-1
unpinch P1
